  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square oil painting of green plant like creatures with beaked heads and single eyes, growing from striped mounds under a canopy of beaded, flowing shapes.",
    "description": "A square oil painting on canvas. The lower half is a thicket of green, teal and lime stalk creatures, each ending in a bulbous head with a single round eye and a beak or tongue, growing from red and green striped mounds along the bottom edge. The upper half is a canopy of flowing leaf and tube shapes edged with strings of tiny coloured beads, in mint, blue, tan and purple, with a few orange and red faces at the top corners. Thick black outlines, strong brushwork, dense all over.",
    "impression": "A greenhouse where the plants have opinions. The beaded edges make the upper forms look like coral or circuitry, and the eyed stalks below look up at them like a congregation. The title's invented word captures the mix of organ, plant and plastic.",
